  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 126 PM CDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nUpper ridging continues to be our primary weather maker through most \nof the work week. Below the ridge, temperatures Wednesday and \nThursday top out in the upper 70s to upper 80s. Heading into the \nweekend, an upper level storm system swings over the western CONUS \nand toward our region, shoving the ridge eastward. Lowering heights \ndrop temperatures back a few degrees Friday compared to the previous \ncouple of days. By Sunday, highs look to range within the 60s and \n70s. Lows most nights are forecast to fall into the mid 50s to low \n60s. The next storm system also brings low to medium (20-60%) rain \nchances to portions of our area Thursday night through Saturday. The \nbest odds will tend to favor our western counties.",
